       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is double the usual maximum. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity.\n\nWas this a typo? These are some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg/day total.** This could be 850 mg PO twice daily, or about 567 mg three times daily, though that isn't a standard tablet strength.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO with meals**, depending on whether this is a new start or a titration.\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
