       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this one as written. Confirming it didn't change the problem. 5,100 mg/day is double the maximum daily dose, and I can't think of a clinical situation where that dose is appropriate. It carries a real risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis. You also haven't given a rationale, and I don't want to put an order like this into the system on my own.\n\nI can enter either of these right away:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **A lower dose** that fits your plan, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n\nIf you think 1,700 mg three times daily is correct, please talk to pharmacy or your attending first. They can verify it and enter it through a pathway that includes that review. If the number came from a unit mix-up, such as 1,700 mg/day, tell me and I'll fix it."
      }
